// MachineRunConsumptionReason Why a recorded run's consumption is not (fully) recorded. artifact_not_found_on_printer: the printer reported no 3MF or it was not on its storage; artifact_on_internal_storage: the print was started from the printer's internal storage, which the connector cannot read (reported while the run is still running and wins over run_in_progress; detail is the internal path as a snake_case code, for example data_metadata_plate_1_gcode); artifact_retrieval_failed: FTPS authentication, listing or transfer failed (detail names the diagnostic); artifact_upload_failed: the connector could not upload the 3MF; artifact_rejected: Core refused the 3MF (parser error, detail is the code); no_slicer_weights_in_artifact: the 3MF has no per-filament weights; gcode_estimate_unavailable: no defensible G-code checkpoint estimate; cancelled_before_first_layer: the print ended before the first layer; outcome_unknown: the run ended without a trustworthy final state and nothing was reported; slot_without_spool_assignment: the printer slot had no mounted spool; no_spool_mapping: a line could not be mapped to a printer slot; connector_offline_during_run: the printer connection or the connector was lost during the run; inventory_not_booked: the lines are resolved but inventory refused the booking (for example no stock); consumption_pending: the connector is still working on it; run_in_progress: the run has not ended; consumption_not_reported: the connector reported nothing and gave no reason (older connector); segment_quantity_unavailable: a line was fed by several spools and its quantity could not be split between them; segment_without_spool: a segment of a line fed by several spools resolved to no spool at its start.
type MachineRunConsumptionReason string

